    "caption": "King Charles says his mother practiced wearing a crown at bath time, because you have to get used to how heavy it is. The Imperial State Crown, which she wore to leave Westminster Abbey after her coronation, was made by Garrard in 1937 for King George VI. It weighs just over a kilogram, holds 2,868 diamonds and has the 317.4 carat Cullinan II in its front band. In a 2018 documentary she said that if she looked down in a crown, her neck would break.",
